- **Body fields that carry the format (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER, `document.ts` at main; re-derive by program, do not trust this list):** `EngagementCreate.due_date`, `EngagementPatch.due_date`, `GuidedEngagementCreate.due_date`, `CloneCreate.due_date`, `FrameworksPut.effective_date`, `ExceptionCreate.review_date` and `.expiry_date`, `EngagementGovernancePut.pilot_date / production_approval_date / next_review_date` (these three are nullable: `oneOf` date or null, so year 0000 must also be refused INSIDE the nullable wrapper). Response schemas (`Engagement`, `Exception`, `VersionException`, `Frameworks`, `Dashboard`) carry the same format: say in DESIGN whether your change reaches the response/contract-check side of the test harness (`apps/api/test/contract.ts`) and why that is or is not a problem.
